ot implemented.\n\nFIX: revise SECURITY.md:26-30 to say the shipped `lore validate` lint proves commands parse and answer, while it cannot prove recovery succeeds and does not constitute operator attestation. Do not claim a weekly schedule or operator-attestation feature is shipped.\n\nch:trace row=DOC-9 spec=SECURITY.md#Threat-notes-specific-to-this-tool wave=none:serial-doc-lane test=none:security-doc-status-claim doc=SECURITY.md evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/lore/audit-lore-docs-2026-10-26-22-41-25.md witness=none:security-prose-and-local-cli-are-self-owned verdict=none:not-judged commit=9acf205df371996b27bfd640bf25ce88100c77ee memory=none:not-written", "capability_tags": ["docs"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-26T22:48:13.844875+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-28T20:33:36+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b8856f29c68965abbce2d1a6ead35c35f371c81fa3db4011ce67b631c561233c", "evidence": [{"run_id":"6c13ee00","ts":"2026-10-28T20:33:36+00:00"}]}, "foreman_note": null, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "fb9c6826064081bab80a51213cdf7d429c1d68cb", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "completed_at": "2026-10-28T20:33:36Z", "worker_summary": "ch:trace row=DOC-9 spec=none:no-spec-anchor-doc-row wave=.coding-hermes/waves/lore-foreman-2026-10-28-19-50-37.json test=none:doc-prose-row doc=SECURITY.md evidence=grep-re-validation-planned-0 lore-validate-count-2 attestation-count-2 witness=none:doc-grep-is-our-own-record verdict=6c13ee00 commit=fb9c6826064081bab80a51213cdf7d429c1d68cb memory=none:no-memory-write STATUS: complete TIER: T1 EVIDENCE: tier2 judge PASS (6c13ee00, commit 67d1fad): marker resolved from this row; attestation distinction preserved; grep counts 0/2/2.", "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: SECURITY.md no longer calls re-validation planned or not implemented; it accurately names `lore validate` as shipped and preserves the separate statement that operator attestation/recovery success are not proved. `grep -nE 're-validation \\(planned|planned, not yet implemented' SECURITY.md` returns 0, while `grep -n 'lore validate' SECURITY.md` returns at least one reader-facing reference.", "acceptance": "PASS: SECURITY.md no longer claims re-validation is planned or not implemented: cd /home/kara/get-h3/lore && grep -ciE \"re-validation \\(planned\" SECURITY.md exits 1 with 0 matching lines, while grep -c \"lore validate\" SECURITY.md returns a count >= 1. The revised text keeps the distinction that the shipped lore validate lint proves commands parse and answer but does not prove recovery succeeds and is not operator attestation (grep -c attestation SECURITY.md >= 1).", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/lore-DOC-9", "branch": "wt/DOC-9"}
